The {{nihongo|'''Tedorigawa Line'''|手取川線|Tedorigawa-sen}} is a subway line in [[Okami|Okami (大紙)]], [[Okaiken]], operated by [[Okami Metro]]. Named after the major river it parallels, the line serves as a strategic "Waterfront Connector," linking the Okami Bay Area directly to the northern transport hubs of [[Fukushima Ward, Okami|Fukushima]] and [[Nakatsu Station|Nakatsu]]. On system maps, the line is color-coded dark brown ({{Okami Metro color|T}}), and its stations use the prefix "T".

The Tedorigawa Line is unique for being the only "River-side" subway in the network. It was constructed to redevelop the former industrial warehouse districts along the riverbanks into modern residential and commercial zones ("River City Okami"). Because it runs through soft alluvial soil near the river, the tunnels were constructed using advanced shield-boring technology.

==History==
Proposed during the "Waterfront Renaissance" project of the 1990s, the Tedorigawa Line was built to bypass the congested city center loops for commuters traveling from the bay to the northern districts.

The entire line from [[Osakako-Tedori Station|Osakako-Tedori]] to [[Nakatsu-Kawaramachi Station|Nakatsu-Kawaramachi]] opened on August 1, 2000. It quickly became a favorite route for tourists visiting the aquarium and theme parks in the bay area, offering a direct link to the northern hotels without transferring through the busy [[Umeda-Kita]] or [[Okami Central]] complexes.

